```

---

### Services/LogAnalyzer.cs

| # | Severity | Description |
|---|----------|-------------|
| 1 | 🔴 Critical | **`new Regex()` per log line** in `TryParseLine` (line 50). For a 100K line log file, this creates 100K+ regex objects. Catastrophic for throughput. |
| 2 | 🟡 Moderate | **Second `new Regex()` per line** for key-value parsing (line 65) and common log format (line 75). |
| 3 | 🟡 Moderate | **`.ToUpper()` allocates** (line 59) — could store level strings as-is or use `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`. |
| 4 | 🟡 Moderate | **Three separate iterations over entries** in `Analyze` (lines 103-125). One pass would suffice. |
| 5 | 🟡 Moderate | **`Skip(i).Take(5).ToList()`** in anomaly detection loop (line 157). Creates a new list on each iteration — should use array indexing. |
| 6 | 🟡 Moderate | **`ContainsKey` + indexer** throughout (lines 105, 112, 129-131, 206-208). |
| 7 | 🟡 Moderate | **String concatenation in `Summarize`** (lines 219-252). Large multi-line report built with `+=`. |
| 8 | ℹ️ Info | **`double.Parse` without `TryParse`** (line 170). Will throw `FormatException` on malformed data. |
| 9 | ℹ️ Info | **`new Regex` per call** in `ExtractErrorCodes` (line 197). Should be `static readonly`. |

**Fix recommendations:**

